---
/* Section 6 — Gap-circle transition.  Slot S6.1.  Motion: ANIMATION-SPEC §6 (play-once: circle grows 0→400→covers viewport, outCubic). */
---
<section class="gap-transition" id="gap" data-gap>
  <div class="gap-circle" data-gap-circle aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <p class="gap-caption animate-text_opacity">Most founders solve this by hiring. First an admin. Then a GM. Then a head of ops. Here's what it hides.</p> <!-- S6.1 — content §5 intro, verbatim -->
</section>

<style>
  .gap-transition {
    position: relative; overflow: hidden;
    min-height: 78vh; display: grid; place-items: center; text-align: center;
    background: var(--paper);
  }
  .gap-circle {
    position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; translate: -50% -50%;
    width: 0; aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--green);
    opacity: 0; will-change: width, opacity;
  }
  html.no-js .gap-circle { width: min(120vw, 1600px); opacity: 1; }
  .gap-caption {
    position: relative; z-index: 2;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 500;
    font-size: var(--title-s); line-height: 1.25; max-width: 22ch; padding-inline: var(--pad-x);
    color: var(--ink); mix-blend-mode: normal;
  }
  html.no-js .gap-caption { color: #fff; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .gap-circle { width: min(120vw, 1600px); opacity: 1; }
    .gap-caption { color: #fff; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) { .gap-transition { min-height: 60vh; } }
</style>
